  "conclusion": "There are TWO distinct generating phases and the shipped signal covers only the second. Phase 1 (thinking) is marked by thinking-dots-animation inside a pending-request container; phase 2 (streaming) by aria-busy on a model-response. A correct 'is Gemini working right now' predicate has to OR the two. This file records the observation; it does not change the code.",
  "selector_corrections": {
    "note": "Recorded because a wrong search produced a false negative during this capture, and a false negative written into a fixture becomes a fabricated observation.",
    "wrong": "document.querySelectorAll('lottie-player, lottie-airo') -> 0",
    "right": "document.querySelectorAll('[lottie-animation]') -> 1, and its element is <div lottie-animation class=\"thinking-dots-animation\">",
    "lesson": "An element with a dash in the name is not always a custom element tag. thinking-dots-animation IS a tag, but the lottie inside it is a plain div carrying an attribute. Searching for a tag name that does not exist yields a confident zero."
  },
  "_remeasured_2026_10_02": {
    "why": "The handoff claimed sendButtonFallback 'matched zero elements in every captured state'. That was measured against an EMPTY editor, where Gemini renders no send control at all - so both selectors returned nothing and the fallback looked dead for an unrelated reason. Re-measured with text present.",
    "how": "Kapture `elements` on /app/101e3a288e0253c3, visible=all, one character typed into #ql-editor, then cleared. No script injection used.",
    "empty_editor": {
      "primary_arrow_upward": 0,
      "fallback_send_button": 0,
      "note": "Neither exists. Any conclusion about the fallback drawn here is unsound."
    },
    "with_text": {
      "primary": "input-area-v2 button:has(mat-icon[data-mat-icon-name='arrow_upward'])",
      "primary_matched": 1,
      "primary_element": "button.mdc-icon-button.mat-mdc-icon-button",
      "fallback": "input-area-v2 button.send-button, input-area-v2 [data-test-id='send-button']",
      "fallback_matched": 1,
      "fallback_element": "gem-icon-button.send-button",
      "fallback_classes": "send-button ng-tns-c2197198206-4 has-input submit gem-button gem-button-badge-size-small gem-button-size-small gem-button-type-on-surface lm-enabled",
      "same_bounds": true,
      "bounds": {
        "x": 919.5,
        "y": 594,
        "width": 32,
        "height": 32
      },
      "relationship": "The fallback resolves the Angular gem-icon-button wrapper; the primary resolves the inner button. Same control, two independent hooks."
    },
    "decision": "KEEP the fallback and correct the contract. It is not providing nothing - it is a hook on a different element that survives a Material internals change, which is what it was added for. The contract's observed:false is the thing that was wrong.",
    "still_wrong_in_this_file": "states.filled records the arrow_upward mat-icon but omits BOTH its parent button and the gem-icon-button.send-button wrapper, so the recorded tree could not have produced the fallback's match. That omission is what let the zero-match claim look credible."
  }
